      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-17_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>Warrington Photographic Society.</head>
        <p>Warrington Photographic Society.</p>
        <p>The evolution of the Briclgo is a subject specially interesting to Warringtonians at pre- sent, and being dealt with by an expert, the Surveyor to the Runcorn Council, was, on Tuesday, made doubly so. Mr. Wilding, by means of a splendid series of lantern pictures, traced bridge construction from the single-stone bridges on Dartmoor to the latest phase of the engineer's science in ferro-concrete. In intro- ducing the Suspension Bridge, some flesh-creep- ing instances of rope bridges in /ndia were shown, and a remarkable bridge in the same rugged country illustrating the elements of the cantilever principle served to introduce a splendid series of pictures showing the growth of the Pnrth Bridge. Mr. WOrlina has his subject so well in hand that although much of the loch-ire dealt with the severely teehninal side of bridgegibuilding, the interest of his hearers never flagged, and a hearty vote of thanks was . accorded to Wm</p>
        <p>_</p>
      </div>
