        <p>Tradesmen's Association.—The annual meeting of the Lymm Tradesmen's ABBOCIUtIOII was held on Tuesday, when Mr. W. E. Miller presided. Mr. Daniels, the secretary, and Mr. F. E. Evans, elle treasurer pro. tem., read their reports, and both were considered satisfactory. Toe ejection of officers resulted_injilr. Daniels being elected the president for next year, with Mr. W. E. Hillier as hon. secretary and Mr. A. V. Richard- son as hon.. treasurer. The committee was re- elected en' bloc.</p>
        <p>L. -- Lion se, deal of report, After that it las 3 his gra that tl out in the eta to do</p>
        <p>Congregational Scholars' Tea.—The Congrega- tional School waf+ the Centre of gay scenes on Thursday and Friday evenings, the occasion being the scholars' annual tea. On the former night the elder scholars participated in an ex- cellent repast, after which the prize distribution took place, Mrs. Penaliggon gracefully making the presentations. A miscellaneous programme was enjoyed. and in t• re co t bated by Elsie Miller and Sydgey Wright, and Mr. H. Hesketh performed a number of excellent tricks. Games were then inclaigect tit. I,uay the infants were to the fore. Each child was the fortunate recipient of an article of clothing an,' a toy from the Christmas tree. Amongst tlo • who assisted in entertaining the children v-ert• Mesdames Penaliggon and Willan; the Misses Hesketh and Leah; Rev. J. A. Penaliggon, Messrs. J. Holt, H. Hesketh, J. D. B. Smith, A. Thomas and G. Willan.</p>
