        <p>WARRINGTON UNION. ASSISTANT SCHOOLMASTER. The Guardians invite for the Application _ appointment of ASSISTANT SCHOOLMASTER at their Padgate Schools, near Warrington. s Salary, X6O per annum, together with rations, residence and washing (valued at £4O per annum). List of duties, which include certain additional duties to that of teaching, may be obtained from the Superintendent; of the Homes. Applications to be made upon forms to be obtained from the undersigned, by forwarding slt,ule.isedra7itvheed2bnyh a stamped addressed envelope, arid the same mdea January on Tuesday, rylatel9rl4th. an 10 a.m. Canvassing the Guardians either directly or indirectly will disqualify. By order, . ARTII Cit BOTTOMLEY, Clerk. Unioi Offices, Bewsey Chambers, Warrington, 14th January, 1914.</p>
        <p>lAtt AMNI TC ET E . INA cIiOirsAHLIREIIIENASLUTRIAINCIENSCUO MEDICAL BENEFIT. The Insurance Committee for the County Palatine of Chester HEREBY GIVES NOTICE PO INSURED PERSONS resident within the Administrative County that the following arrangements for Medical Benefit have been made for the year commencing the 12th January, 1914, : Red ISledical Tickets and Forms, "Med. 32," are no longer available for the purpose of choos- ing a Doctor or Institution, and will not be accepted. Medical Cards issued by the Insur- ance Committee must be used instead. If an Insured -Person has not yet selected a Doctor or Institution on the Panel List, appli- cation should be made for a Medical Card to me, the undersigned, on a form (Med. 50), which can be obtained from any Post Office. Upon receiving the, Medical Card, Insured Persons should, WITHOUT DELAY, give the same to the Doctor on the Panel or Institution he wishes to select. Insured Persons should not delay doing so until they are ill. - Insured Persons already on the list of a Doctor or Inie-itution will, in due course, WITHOUT MARINO APPLICATION, receive a Medical Card from the Insurance Committee hearing the name of the Doctor or Institution, and after the Medical Card has been issued, it must be produced to the Doctor or Institution whenever the Insured Person requires treat- ment. Tile Medical Card will contain information n q to the Stens to be taken to enable insured Persons to obtain Medical Benefit on change of n ress . The New Medical List of Doctors, Chemists. fi nil institutions will shortly be available at all Post Offices in the ConimittPe's area. FRANK 'P. WEST, Clerk to the Committee. 100 Nort'hgate-street, Chester, • 14th January. 1914.</p>
