        <p>COUNTY COUNCIL OF LANCASHIRE. TENDERS FOR STATIONERY, &amp;c. The Finance Committee of the County Coun- cil of Lancashire invite TENDERS for the Supply of the STATIONERY, &amp;c., required at the County Offices, Preston, from Ist April, 1914, to 31st March. 1915. Forms of Tender and Specifications and all information may be obtained, and samples seen, on application to the Stationery Clerk, County Offices, Preston, on or after 26th January. Sealed Tenders, en- dorsed "Tenders for Stationery," and addressed to the Chairman of the Finance Committee, must be delivered at the County Offices, Preston, not later than Tuesday, the 17th February, 1914. The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. HARCOURT E. CLARE, Clerk to the County Council. County Offices, Preston, January 17th, 1914.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. TO BUTT HERS. The TOWN HALL, PARKS and BATHS COM- MITTEE of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive TENDERS for the Erection of Boiler-house Chimney. and alterations at the Baths in Bath-street. Draw- ings. specifications, &amp;c., may be seen, and forms of tender, bills of quantities, and all further in- formation obtained at the office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on and after Tuesday, the 20th inst., at which place tenders must be de- livered before 12 o'clock noon on Monday, the 2nd day of February, 1914. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accented. ANDREW M. KER, Borough Engineer and Surveyor. liorough Engineer and Surveyor's Office, 16th January, 1914. ,</p>
