        <p>Marriages. MAGENIS—GREEN.—On the 3rd of December, at St. Mary Magdalene's Church, Adelaide, South Australia, by the Rev. Canon C. S. Hornahrook, George Charles Magenis, late of Warrington, to Margaret, youngest daughter of Mr.. and Mrs. John Green, of 15, Lairs-street, Warrington. BRAYSHAW—CHESTER.---On Thursday, 15th inst., at St. James' Church, by the Rev. H. B. Firth, Arthur Brayshaw, of Wilderspool-road, to Emily Chester, of Bridge-street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>Deaths. . LOCKER.—Jannary Bth, at 104, Knntsford-road, George Locker, aged 33 years. FALLON.—January 9th, at 11, Litherland-yard, Margaret Fallon, aged 62 years.</p>
        <p>In Memoriam. PATRICK.—In loving memory of Mary Ann Patrick, who died at GG, Wellington-street, War- rington, January 11th, 1913. Sadly missed. ALBERT and GEORGE. HASSALL.—In loving memory of our dear son and brother, Sam Hassall, of Elmhurst, Latchford Without, who passed away on January 16th, 1913. Oh. for a touch of a vanished hand, And a sound of a voice that is still. 44, Thewlis-street Warrington.</p>
